+++
title: Ptolemaic synodal decrees
description: Ancient Egyptian religious decrees
hook: "In each of these decrees a synod of Egyptian priests set down what
  their Greek king had done for the temples, and voted him honours in return:
  statues, shrines, worship as a god. Nine of the decrees are known, from 243
  BC to 161 BC, and one of the stones cut with them is the Rosetta Stone."
standfirst: Nine decrees, from 243 BC to 161 BC, in which Egypt's priests
  honoured four Greek kings for what they had given the temples. The stones
  carrying them have been turning up since 1799, when the Rosetta Stone was
  found, and the latest surfaced in 2004.
